course: dictionary
lesson: 11299
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is right by reading the words around it, which is the context. «The puppy yapped at the postman.» Here yapped means a small dog gave short, sharp barks.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another sentence. «Stop yapping!» means someone is talking a lot, loudly or in a silly way. A dog yaps, and a person can yap too when they chatter on and on.
explain: Be careful with rude words. «Shut your yap!» is rude slang for your mouth, so never say it to a teacher. Some words are also names of places: «On the island of Yap, giant stone wheels were used as money.»
fact: Yap can be a verb (it yaps, yapped, yapping) or a noun (a yap is a short, sharp bark).
fact: «Yap» means to give short, high, sharp barks, as a small dog does.
fact: «Yap» can also mean to talk a lot, loudly or in a silly way.
fact: «Shut your yap» is rude slang, so do not say it to teachers or other grown-ups.
fact: «Yappy» describes a dog that yaps a lot.
exercise: «The puppy yapped at the postman.» What does yapped mean here? | Ate a big dinner | *Gave short, sharp barks | Went to sleep in the sun | Carried a parcel up the path
exercise: «Stop yapping, Sam, I am trying to read.» What does yapping mean here? | Sleeping softly | Swimming in the pond | *Talking a lot, loudly or in a silly way | Running very fast
exercise: A tiny dog gives one short, sharp bark. What is the noun for that bark? | a yard | *a yap | a yawn | a yolk
test: Why should you not say «Shut your yap!» to a teacher? | *It is rude slang, so it is impolite to a teacher | It is the name of a dog | It is a polite greeting | It means well done
test: In «On the island of Yap, giant stone wheels were used as money.» what kind of word is Yap? | A verb | A noun for a bark | A type of dog | *A place name
exam: «Yappy» describes a dog that does what? | Sleeps all day | Reads books in the library | Swims in the sea | *Yaps a lot
